# Electrical Concepts to Learn

### Fundamental Quantities & Material Physics
* **Electric Charge & Coulombs:** How electrons carry charge and how net charge creates an electric field.
* **Drift Velocity vs. Field Speed:** Why electrons drift at fractions of a millimeter per second, while electric signals travel at near the speed of light.
* **Electric Potential Difference / Voltage:** Work done per unit charge to move current through a circuit.
* **Current:** Rate of charge flow measured in Amperes; direct current (DC) vs. alternating current (AC).
* **Conductors, Insulators, and Semiconductors:**
  * **Conductors:** Overlapping valence and conduction bands (free electron "sea").
  * **Insulators:** Large forbidden energy bandgap blocking electron movement.
  * **Semiconductors:** Narrow bandgap allowing thermal excitation and doping.

---

### Resistance, Conductance & Basic DC Laws
* **Resistivity & Geometric Resistance:** Wire gauge (AWG) selection to avoid line resistance.
* **Ohm’s Law:** Linear relationship in ohmic materials.
* **Joule’s Law & Power Dissipation:** Calculating heat limits to avoid burning resistors, PCB traces, or motor windings.
* **Kirchhoff’s Current Law (KCL):** Conservation of charge at circuit junctions.
* **Kirchhoff’s Voltage Law (KVL):** Conservation of energy around closed loops.
* **Series and Parallel Networks:** Equivalent resistance across components.
* **Voltage Dividers:** Dropping voltages for analog sensing.
* **Current Dividers:** Splitting parallel current paths.

---

### Energy Storage Elements (Capacitance & Inductance)
* **Capacitance & Electrostatic Fields:**
  * Current-voltage relationship across a capacitor.
  * **Decoupling/Bypass Capacitors:** Suppressing voltage drops and brownouts during sudden motor start currents.
  * **RC Circuits:** Time constant, low-pass and high-pass filtering of analog sensor signals.
* **Inductance & Magnetic Fields:**
  * Magnetic flux, Faraday’s Law, and Lenz’s Law.
  * Inductor voltage relationship with rate of change of current.
  * **Inductive Kickback:** High-voltage spikes created when current through a motor or relay coil drops instantly to zero.
  * **RL Circuits:** Time constant and energizing/de-energizing transient states.

---

### Magnetism, Torque & Motor Electromechanics
* **Lorentz Force Law:** How current-carrying wires inside a magnetic field produce physical force.
* **Electromagnetic Torque:** Converting electrical power to mechanical rotation using motor torque constants.
* **Back-Electromotive Force (Back-EMF):** Motors acting as generators when spinning, limiting top speed.
* **Stall Current & Winding Resistance:** Peak current draw when a motor or robotic arm is forced to stop moving.

---

### Circuit Analysis & Power Supply Basics
* **Internal Resistance of Batteries:** Why a battery terminal voltage sags under heavy loads.
* **Grounding Principles:** Star ground vs. ground loops; isolating dirty motor grounds from clean microcontroller logic grounds.
* **Linear Regulators vs. Switching (Buck/Boost) Regulators:** Stepping down higher battery voltages efficiently without thermal damage.


